# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers static assets.
# Lands at dist/_headers via publicDir; parsed by Workers, never served as an asset.
#
# CORRECTION: these two WERE assumed to come from the Cloudflare zone, and they do
# not. Measured immediately after the DNS cutover, both vanished — a zone-level
# setting would have kept firing regardless of origin, so they were being sent by the
# old shared host's server config all along. Restored here verbatim as the old origin
# sent them; nothing more is added, to avoid changing behaviour beyond what was lost.
#
# The durable home for HSTS is the zone setting (SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates -> HSTS),
# which also covers redirects and error responses that never reach this Worker. If it
# is enabled there, REMOVE the header from here — applying it twice risks a
# comma-joined value.

# Content-hashed by Astro, so the filename changes whenever the bytes do — safe to
# cache forever. Everything else keeps the default `max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# which is what HTML wants and yields cheap ETag 304s.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
